---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="METHODOLOGY — PURSUE://INDEX"
  description="How the pursueindex manifest is built: ingest, hashing, OCR, and diff."
  active="methodology"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="space-y-2 border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)] pb-4">
      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)] flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">$</span>
        <span>man pursue-index</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-mono font-semibold tracking-tight text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">
        METHODOLOGY
      </h1>
    </header>

    <section class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 pi-bracket relative scanlines-soft space-y-3">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Each release is fetched directly from the canonical
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">war.gov</code>
        CSV, normalized into a typed manifest, hashed (SHA-256), and committed
        alongside its prior snapshot. PDFs are fetched once and pinned by
        URL; OCR is performed locally (Surya GPU pipeline; Tesseract
        fallback) and benchmarked against a golden-set before a release
        ships. Every claim in the search index can be traced back to a
        specific page and the underlying public-domain source.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Full methodology — engine choice, confidence thresholds, redaction
        handling, correction workflow — will be published before the v1.0
        public launch.
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)] pt-2">
        DOC · <span class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">DRAFT</span>
        <span class="mx-2">·</span>
        REV · <span class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">0.1</span>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
